  {
    "name": "make_polygon_face",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "points": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 3,
          "description": "corners in order: point names or \"x,y,z\""
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "points"
      ]
    },
    "description": "Planar face bounded by a closed polygon through `points` (3 or more corners, in order; the last joins back to the first). Extrude it with make_prism for a gable roof, wedge or any prismatic profile. Straight sides only: for an outline with arcs or curves use make_profile_face.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_arc",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "start": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "start point"
        },
        "end": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "end point (centre form: sets the direction only)"
        },
        "center": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "centre point (centre form)"
        },
        "through": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "a point the arc passes through, between start and end (3-point form)"
        },
        "reverse": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "centre form: take the longer way round"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "start",
        "end"
      ]
    },
    "description": "A circular arc edge, in one of two forms: `center` + `start` + `end` (radius = centre to start; `end` only sets the direction the arc stops at; it takes the shorter way round, `reverse` the longer; for a half circle use the other form) or `start` + `through` + `end` (the arc passes through all three). Points are names or \"x,y,z\". The result gives the arc's real end points and length: start the next segment there. Chain arcs and make_line segments with make_wire, then make_face_from_wires; for a whole outline make_profile_face does it in one call.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_wire",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "edges": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "edges or wires, each touching the next"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "edges"
      ]
    },
    "description": "Join edges (make_line, make_arc, ... segments) end to end into one wire. The result says whether it is closed; a closed wire can be made into a face with make_face_from_wires.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_face_from_wires",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "wires": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "description": "outer contour first, then holes"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "wires"
      ]
    },
    "description": "Planar face bounded by closed wires: the first is the outer contour, any others are holes (make_wire results, or a make_circle edge for a round hole). Extrude it with make_prism or revolve it with make_revolution.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_ellipse",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "center": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "centre point"
        },
        "normal": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "normal of the ellipse plane (full form)"
        },
        "r_major": {
          "type": "number",
          "description": "major radius (full form)"
        },
        "r_minor": {
          "type": "number",
          "description": "minor radius, <= r_major (full form)"
        },
        "major_dir": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "direction of the major axis (full form)"
        },
        "start": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "end of one semi-axis (quarter form)"
        },
        "end": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "end of the other semi-axis (quarter form)"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "center"
      ]
    },
    "description": "An ellipse edge, in one of two forms: `center` + `normal` + `r_major` + `r_minor` (a full ellipse; `major_dir` orients the major axis) or `center` + `start` + `end` (a quarter ellipse from `start` to `end`, two points at right angles from the centre at the ends of the semi-axes). Points are names or \"x,y,z\".",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_polyline",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "points": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 2,
          "description": "point names or \"x,y,z\", in order"
        },
        "closed": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "points"
      ]
    },
    "description": "A wire of straight segments through `points` in order; `closed` joins the last back to the first. Open, it is a path for make_pipe or a piece for make_wire; for a filled polygon use make_polygon_face.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_curve",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "points": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 2,
          "description": "point names or \"x,y,z\", in order"
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "interpolation",
            "bezier"
          ],
          "default": "interpolation"
        },
        "closed": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false
        },
        "start_tangent": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "direction at the first point"
        },
        "end_tangent": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "direction at the last point"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "points"
      ]
    },
    "description": "A smooth curve edge from `points`: kind \"interpolation\" (default) passes through every point, \"bezier\" only through the first and last (the others pull it like control points). `closed` makes a loop; `start_tangent` + `end_tangent` (directions, open interpolation only) set the direction at the ends. The result gives its real end points and length.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
  {
    "name": "make_profile_face",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "start": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "point name or \"x,y,z\""
        },
        "segments": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "to": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "where the segment ends"
              },
              "center": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "circular arc about this centre (shorter way round)"
              },
              "reverse": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "default": false,
                "description": "centre arc: the longer way round"
              },
              "through": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "circular arc through this point"
              },
              "via": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "smooth curve through these points"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "to"
            ]
          }
        },
        "holes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "start": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "point name or \"x,y,z\""
              },
              "segments": {
                "type": "array",
                "minItems": 1,
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "to": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "where the segment ends"
                    },
                    "center": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "circular arc about this centre (shorter way round)"
                    },
                    "reverse": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                      "default": false,
                      "description": "centre arc: the longer way round"
                    },
                    "through": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "circular arc through this point"
                    },
                    "via": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "description": "smooth curve through these points"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "to"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "center": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "round hole centre"
              },
              "radius": {
                "type": "number",
                "description": "round hole radius"
              },
              "wire": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "name of an existing closed wire"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "an outline ({start, segments}), a circle ({center, radius}) or {wire}"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "start",
        "segments"
      ]
    },
    "description": "Planar face from an outline traced from `start` through `segments`, each starting where the previous one ends and ending at its `to`: a straight line, or a circular arc with `center` (shorter way round, `reverse` for the longer; for a half circle give `through` instead) or `through` (a point on the arc), or a smooth curve through `via` points. If the last `to` is not back at `start` a straight line closes it. `holes`: outlines of the same form, {\"center\", \"radius\"} circles, or {\"wire\": name} of a closed wire. Builds edges, wire and face in one call: prefer it to make_line/make_arc/make_wire/make_face_from_wires for a whole outline. Extrude it with make_prism or revolve it with make_revolution.",
    "category": "sketch"
  },
